  "text": "Recipe: Sweet Potato Chaat\nCreator: Kiran Sharma\nCategory: Chaat\nIngredients: sweet potatoes, paprika, 21 Seasoning Salute Blend, black pepper powder, dried parsley, Garlic Tahini, blackstrap molasses, chickpeas, sweet corn, pomegranate seeds\nCooking methods: bake, boil, no-cook\nInstructions: PREP: (a) Preheat the oven to 420F. (b) Scrub the sweet potatoes clean. I left the peel on.\nCook sweet potatoes partially. I cooked them in a pressure cooker (opened 5 minutes after the first whistle). At this point, sweet potatoes were half cooked.\nChop the half cooked sweet potatoes into fries of any shape; wedges with thickness 1/2\" to 3/4\" are recommended.\nToss sweet potato wedges into a large bowl. Sprinkle some water and any seasonings of your choice. Mix well.\nPlace the seasoned wedges inside a baking tray lined with a Silicone Mat, making sure they do not touch.\nBake for 35-40 minutes. Turn them over after 20 minutes. Cook them until they turn golden brown and crispy.\nServe with Garlic Tahini, a drizzle of blackstrap molasses along with toasted chickpeas, corn, and pomegranate seeds.\nNotes: Sprinkling some water on sweet potato wedges, helps the seasoning to adhere and avoid burning.",
